comments_summary.body:
![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)

If `getWorstSlack()` is called before a RAM block has been generated (e.g., if the user runs `report_ram_timing` on an empty design), `block_` will be `nullptr`. Calling `network_->setBlock(nullptr)` followed by `sta_->updateTiming(false)` will result in a segmentation fault. Adding a defensive check for `block_` prevents this crash.

```c
float RamGen::getWorstSlack()
{
  if (!block_) {
    logger_->warn(utl::RAM, 44, "No RAM block has been generated yet.");
    return 0.0;
  }
  network_->setBlock(block_);
  sta_->updateTiming(false);
  return sta_->worstSlack(sta::MinMax::max());
}
```

![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)

If `getTotalPower()` is called before a RAM block has been generated, `block_` will be `nullptr`. Calling `network_->setBlock(nullptr)` followed by `sta_->updateTiming(false)` will result in a segmentation fault. Adding a defensive check for `block_` prevents this crash.

```c
float RamGen::getTotalPower()
{
  if (!block_) {
    logger_->warn(utl::RAM, 45, "No RAM block has been generated yet.");
    return 0.0;
  }
  network_->setBlock(block_);
  sta_->updateTiming(false);
  sta::PowerResult total, sequential, combinational, clock, macro, pad;
  sta_->power(
      sta_->cmdScene(), total, sequential, combinational, clock, macro, pad);
  return total.total();
}
```

![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

If timing is unconstrained, `get_ram_worst_slack` can return a very large value representing infinity (e.g., `1e30`). Attempting to format this value with `format %.3f` can throw a Tcl error on some platforms. Checking if the slack is unconstrained (e.g., greater than `1e29`) and reporting `N/A` avoids this formatting error.

```
proc report_ram_timing { } {
  set slack [ram::get_ram_worst_slack]
  if { $slack > 1e29 } {
    utl::report "RAM worst setup slack: N/A"
  } else {
    utl::report "RAM worst setup slack: [format %.3f [expr { $slack * 1e9 }]] ns"
  }
}
```

![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)

There are multiple memory leaks in `RamGen::reportTiming()`:

1. **`sta::PinSet` Leaks**: `collect_primary_inputs` and `collect_endpoints` allocate `sta::PinSet` on the heap using `new` but they are never deleted.
2. **`sta::ExceptionFrom` and `sta::ExceptionTo` Leaks**: `sta_->makeExceptionFrom` and `sta_->makeExceptionTo` allocate exception objects on the heap which must be deleted by the caller.
3. **`sta::PathEnd` Leaks**: `sta_->findPathEnds` allocates `PathEnd` objects inside the returned `PathEndSeq` sequence, which must be deleted to avoid leaking memory.

Additionally, `setup_from`/`hold_from` and `setup_to`/`hold_to` are identical and can be consolidated into a single `exception_from` and `exception_to` to avoid redundant allocations.

We can resolve all of these issues by:
- Allocating `sta::PinSet` on the stack and passing their addresses.
- Reusing the exception objects for both setup and hold analysis.
- Explicitly deleting the allocated exceptions and path ends at the end of the function.

```c
double RamGen::reportTiming()
{
  network_->setBlock(block_);
  sta_->updateTiming(false);

  sta::SceneSeq scenes = sta_->makeSceneSeq(sta_->cmdScene());
  sta::StringSeq group_names;

  auto collect_primary_inputs = [&](sta::PinSet& pins) {
    for (auto* bterm : data_inputs_) {
      pins.insert(network_->dbToSta(bterm));
    }
    for (auto& port_addrs : addr_inputs_) {
      for (auto* bterm : port_addrs) {
        pins.insert(network_->dbToSta(bterm));
      }
    }
    for (auto* bterm : write_enable_) {
      pins.insert(network_->dbToSta(bterm));
    }
  };

  auto collect_endpoints = [&](sta::PinSet& pins) {
    for (auto* inst : block_->getInsts()) {
      for (auto* iterm : inst->getITerms()) {
        auto* pin = network_->dbToSta(iterm);
        if (!pin || isClockPin(pin, network_)) {
          continue;
        }
        auto* lp = network_->libertyPort(pin);
        if (lp && (lp->direction()->isAnyOutput() || lp->isClockGateEnable())) {
          pins.insert(pin);
        }
      }
    }
    for (auto* bterm : block_->getBTerms()) {
      auto* pin = network_->dbToSta(bterm);
      if (pin && !isClockPin(pin, network_)
          && network_->direction(pin)->isOutput()) {
        pins.insert(pin);
      }
    }
  };

  sta::PinSet primary_inputs(network_);
  collect_primary_inputs(primary_inputs);

  sta::PinSet endpoints(network_);
  collect_endpoints(endpoints);

  // Find worst unconstrained setup path delay/longest path
  sta::ExceptionFrom* exception_from
      = sta_->makeExceptionFrom(&primary_inputs,
                                nullptr,
                                nullptr,
                                sta::RiseFallBoth::riseFall(),
                                sta_->cmdSdc());

  sta::ExceptionTo* exception_to
      = sta_->makeExceptionTo(&endpoints,
                              nullptr,
                              nullptr,
                              sta::RiseFallBoth::riseFall(),
                              sta::RiseFallBoth::riseFall(),
                              sta_->cmdSdc());

  sta::PathEndSeq setup_ends
      = sta_->findPathEnds(exception_from,            /* from */
                           nullptr,               /* thrus */
                           exception_to,          /* to */
                           true,                  /* unconstrained */
                           scenes,                /* scenes */
                           sta::MinMaxAll::max(), /* min_max */
                           1,                     /* group_path_count */
                           1,                     /* endpoint_path_count */
                           false,                 /* unique_pins */
                           false,                 /* unique_edges */
                           -sta::INF,             /* slack_min */
                           sta::INF,              /* slack_max */
                           true,                  /* sort_by_slack */
                           group_names,           /* group_names */
                           true,                  /* setup */
                           false,                 /* hold */
                           false,                 /* recovery */
                           false,                 /* removal */
                           true,                  /* clk_gating_setup */
                           false);                /* clk_gating_hold */

  float setup_delay
      = setup_ends.empty()
            ? 0.0
            : static_cast<float>(setup_ends[0]->dataArrivalTime(sta_));

  // Find worst unconstrained hold path delay/shortest path
  sta::PathEndSeq hold_ends
      = sta_->findPathEnds(exception_from,             /* from */
                           nullptr,               /* thrus */
                           exception_to,               /* to */
                           true,                  /* unconstrained */
                           scenes,                /* scenes */
                           sta::MinMaxAll::min(), /* min_max */
                           1,                     /* group_path_count */
                           1,                     /* endpoint_path_count */
                           false,                 /* unique_pins */
                           false,                 /* unique_edges */
                           -sta::INF,             /* slack_min */
                           sta::INF,              /* slack_max */
                           true,                  /* sort_by_slack */
                           group_names,           /* group_names */
                           false,                 /* setup */
                           true,                  /* hold */
                           false,                 /* recovery */
                           false,                 /* removal */
                           false,                 /* clk_gating_setup */
                           true);                 /* clk_gating_hold */

  float hold_delay
      = hold_ends.empty()
            ? 0.0
            : static_cast<float>(hold_ends[0]->dataArrivalTime(sta_));

  sta::Unit* time_unit = sta_->units()->timeUnit();
  logger_->info(RAM,
                44,
                "RAM maximum path delay: {} {}",
                time_unit->asString(setup_delay),
                time_unit->scaleAbbrevSuffix());
  logger_->info(RAM,
                45,
                "RAM minimum path delay: {} {}",
                time_unit->asString(hold_delay),
                time_unit->scaleAbbrevSuffix());

  for (auto* end : setup_ends) {
    delete end;
  }
  for (auto* end : hold_ends) {
    delete end;
  }
  delete exception_from;
  delete exception_to;

  if (setup_delay <= 0.0F) {
    return 0.0;
  }
  logger_->info(RAM,
                47,
                "Using maximum path delay of {} {} as the clock period for "
                "power estimation",
                time_unit->asString(setup_delay),
                time_unit->scaleAbbrevSuffix());
  return time_unit->staToUser(setup_delay);
}
```
